-- title:
--   Level-one place specialisation over an arbitrary residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime, and let `data` be a modular-polynomial datum at level $\ell$: a monic polynomial $\Phi$ in $\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ (outer variable $X$, inner variable $Y$) of degree $\psi(\ell)$ in $X$ which vanishes when its coefficients are evaluated at the $q$-expansion of $j$ and $X$ at that of $j(q^{\ell})$. Assume Kronecker's congruence `hKr`: the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $\ell$ equals $(Y^{\ell}-X)(Y-X^{\ell})$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)[X][Y]$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism. Assume `hα` and `hβ`, the integrality of the two ring maps from the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $1$ into that of level $1\cdot\ell$, namely the inclusion coming from the degeneracy at level $\ell$ and the map induced by $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$. Then the type $\mathrm{PlaceSpecialization}$ attached to these data is nonempty: there exists a packet consisting of a map $\mathrm{sp}$ from the places of the level-one modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the places of the $k$-field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$ generated by the reduced $j$-series, an additive map $\mathrm{spPic0}$ from $J_0(1)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of that field, sending, for each place $w$ and each $a \in A$, a zero of $j - a$ to a zero of $\tilde\jmath - \mathrm{red}(a)$ and a place at which $j$ takes no value in $A$ to a pole of $\tilde\jmath$, the analogous conditions for the level-$N$ series with $N = 1$, and the remaining compatibility conditions required by the structure `PlaceSpecialization`.
--
--   This is the level-one instance of the reduction of modular curves and their Jacobians modulo $\ell$ in the style of the Kroneckerian model, with the reduction target allowed to be any field of characteristic $\ell$ receiving $A$ surjectively rather than the canonical residue field of $A$. It supplies the base case of the specialisation machinery used in the level-lowering argument, and is invoked by the results on cuspidal places lying on the infinity or zero Kronecker branch and on separated coverings of charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_placeSpecialization_exists_level_one_of_surjective.lean

